1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,900
Overview — 1.0M real retail transactions: £19.64M revenue, 5,852 customers, 3.6% returns

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:17,900
Spec scoreboard: every target is shown as measured, not claimed

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:26,900
Demand Forecast — Prophet + LSTM ensemble predicts the next 30 trading days

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:44,900
Accuracy: weekly MAPE 11.9% (target ≤ 12%), 30-day total error 4.2%. Daily MAPE stays ~31% because of lumpy wholesale orders

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:53,900
Decomposition: trend + weekly seasonality; the series is non-stationary (ADF test)

6
00:00:54,000 --> 00:01:20,900
What-if scenarios: change promotion, price, market shock or closed days — forecast and revenue update instantly

7
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:38,900
Customer Segments — K-Means finds 6 segments; 'Champions' generate ~73% of revenue

8
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:47,900
3-D cluster map of customers (PCA projection)

9
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:56,900
Model selection: silhouette picks k = 6 (inside the 6–8 band); DBSCAN finds only 2 clusters

10
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:14,900
Customer list: filter by segment. IDs are masked pseudonyms for the Viewer role

11
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:23,900
Churn Prediction — XGBoost tuned with Optuna, compared with Logistic Regression and Random Forest

12
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,900
AUC-ROC 0.806 on a strict out-of-time test (0.88 target not met). Precision in top-20% risk: 0.889 (target met)

13
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:41,900
Churn is seasonal: the base rate swings from ~40% to ~70% across the year

14
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:59,900
At-risk customers: filter by tier, segment and spend. Each row lists its top SHAP risk drivers

15
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:17,900
Retention simulator: budget, cost per contact and save rate give the expected profit

16
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:26,900
Profit curve shows where to stop contacting customers

17
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:44,900
Inventory — reorder points, safety stock, EOQ. Sliders for service level, lead time and demand re-plan instantly (stock levels are simulated)

18
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:53,900
Back-test on 766 real replenishment cycles: RetailPulse 87.4% fill rate vs 70.0% for a naive moving average

19
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:02,900
MLOps — 13 MLflow runs tracked across segmentation, forecast, churn, inventory and drift

20
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:11,900
Drift monitor: PSI per feature compares today's customers with the training reference

21
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:20,900
Drift simulation: the slider injects a market shock; the model is retrained once 30% of features drift

22
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:38,900
Data & ETL — 1,067,371 raw rows → 1,003,336 clean (94%). 27 of 27 data-quality checks pass

23
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:47,900
Source: UCI Online Retail II (CC BY 4.0). Custom column added in ETL: region_group

24
00:04:48,000 --> 00:05:10,900
Role-based access: Viewer by default; Analyst and Admin unlock exports and the audit log

25
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:27,900
Executive PDF report generated from the live results

26
00:05:28,000 --> 00:06:05,200
CSV bundle export: forecast, segments, churn scores, purchase plan and drift table

